  "observations": [
    "Opened and inspected every one of 36 exact-r006 full-angle PNGs: 24 azimuths and all 12 diagnostics. Also inspected the 128px silhouette, 512px hero/clay/detail and 384px crozier attachment. The website poster and all 24 full-resolution 768px WebP orbit frames were decoded losslessly and inspected over a neutral matte; source WebP and decoded PNG hashes match.",
    "Compared immutable 2,418-triangle original and r006 at identical world camera, lighting, color management and framing. The original has broad arrow-shaped pinna shoulders and abrupt angular folds. Refined pinnae narrow gradually along multiple bends, attach visibly to the rachis and have slim tips; the whole frond bends continuously.",
    "Three unequal height tiers and clear inter-frond windows produce a more legible radial crown. No single elevated blade dominates every view. Projected tip crossings vary naturally through the orbit; no welded or abruptly cut terminal-tip defect was visible. Seven stipes/rachises remain traceable toward the one low crown; one small crozier is visibly continuous from its stipe to the coil.",
    "Neutral clay and alternate key retain the structural improvement without green color. Quad-pair normals reduce distracting diagonal faceting in pinna faces while preserving deliberate lowpoly plane changes. At 128px leaves necessarily become fine strokes; the layered whole plant remains readable. This is not a distant-gameplay LOD certification.",
    "Cost is explicitly 7,736 triangles/420,508 bytes/3 primitives versus 2,418 triangles/186,208 bytes original. The added geometry earns curved solid blades, continuous axes and differentiated tiering. Exact geometry and materials match r005, but normals changed, so r006 was reviewed as a new shading/export representation rather than inheriting r005 approval."
  ],
